      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Swatara Creek borders the town, forming its northern and western edges and feeding a pond beside the Nature Trail.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hummelstown%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Warwick Hotel, a tavern that dates back to pre‑Revolutionary War times, still operates in Hummelstown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hummelstown%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Hummelstown’s historic brownstone company once supplied stone for many regional buildings, and its former station still stands on 2nd Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hummelstown%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Hummelstown’s Historical Society, housed in the former Zion Lutheran Church, serves as both a museum and visitor center.",
